# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# J) TTY Config
# Settings specific to the plain-terminal ("tty") interface.

# Use a timer-based pause for momentary display effects (explosions, moving
# objects) instead of sending extra filler characters to the screen to
# create the delay. Applies to the tty and curses interfaces (X11 always
# uses a timer). This is already the compiled-in default when available;
# it's set explicitly here for clarity.
OPTIONS=timed_delay

# SYMBOLS=name:char remaps a single glyph. Full list of symbol names is in
# the `symbols` reference file installed alongside the binary.
SYMBOLS=S_ghost:X
SYMBOLS=S_golem:8
SYMBOLS=S_lava:~
SYMBOLS=S_pool:~
SYMBOLS=S_water:~
SYMBOLS=S_sink:#

# Shorthand for the boulder glyph specifically: replaces the default
# punctuation-mark boulder symbol with the digit '0', which reads more
# clearly as "a big round thing" on most fonts.
OPTIONS=boulder:0

# A couple of extended-character alternatives some players prefer; left
# commented out since they don't render correctly in every terminal/font
# (and not in the curses interface at all).
#SYMBOLS=S_fountain:\xf4
#SYMBOLS=S_tree:\xf1
#SYMBOLS=S_bars:\xf0

# Use bold black instead of blue for "black" glyphs (tty only) -- blue-on-
# black terminal themes can make true black glyphs unreadable otherwise.
OPTIONS=use_darkgray

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# K) Curses Config
# Settings specific to the curses interface. All left commented out except
# where noted, since most players default to the tty interface below; flip
# windowtype to curses and uncomment the rest of this section to switch.

# Enable the curses windowport (default false).
#OPTIONS=windowtype:curses

# This template defaults to tty instead:
OPTIONS=windowtype:tty
OPTIONS=symset:Enhanced1

#OPTIONS=IBMgraphics
#OPTIONS=DECgraphics

# Use the new NH4-style status window layout (true by default where
# supported). Uncomment "!classic_status" to opt back into the old layout.
#OPTIONS=classic_status

# Window borders around the map/status/message panes:
#   1 = always draw borders
#   2 = never draw borders
#   3 = draw borders only if the terminal is big enough (default)
OPTIONS=windowborders:3

# Fix the terminal window to a specific size. Curses will attempt to resize
# to these values but will settle for smaller if the terminal can't fit them.
#OPTIONS=term_cols:124
#OPTIONS=term_rows:32
OPTIONS=term_cols:142
OPTIONS=term_rows:40

# Highlight attribute for pets specifically, distinct from hilite_pet above
# (which is tty/generic); e.g. petattr:i for inverse.
# OPTIONS=petattr:i

# Display detected/remembered monsters (e.g. via monster detection or ESP)
# in an inverse-highlighted manner.
OPTIONS=use_inverse

# Use color in the non-map parts of the screen too (status/message areas).
#OPTIONS=guicolor

# Keep the inventory window permanently visible on the right side of the
# screen, instead of popping it up on demand with 'i'.
OPTIONS=perm_invent

# Message/status pane placement. align_status:left/right gives a more
# verbose, vertically-arranged status display.
#OPTIONS=align_message:top
#OPTIONS=align_status:bottom

# See section G for the full explanation of statuslines; set here since
# it's specifically a tty/curses display setting. 3 shows status conditions
# on their own line and needs a taller (25+ line) terminal; 2 is the
# default, more compact layout.
OPTIONS=statuslines:3

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# X) Other / Misc Config

# What to disclose at the end of a game, and whether to prompt first:
#   i = inventory   a = attributes   v = vanquished monsters
#   g = genocided/exiled monsters    c = conduct    o = dungeon overview
# Prefix each letter with one of:
#   y/n = prompt, defaulting to yes/no     + = disclose without prompting
#   -   = don't disclose, don't prompt
#OPTIONS=disclose:

# How much of the high score list to show at the end of a game.
#OPTIONS=scores:10 top/0 around/

# Print an ASCII tombstone on death.
OPTIONS=tombstone

## A couple of newer options worth knowing about (not NerfHack-exclusive --
# autostairtravel originates from the Hack'EM project, showdamage shipped
# with upstream NetHack 5.0 -- but both are recent enough to be worth
# calling out explicitly here).

# Automatically travel to the nearest stairs when using '<' or '>' instead
# of needing to already be standing on them.
OPTIONS=autostairtravel

# Whenever you take damage, show a message with how much and your
# remaining HP.
OPTIONS=showdamage
